The next checkpoint should reconstruct the documented BMC Finance workflow at task level:

```text
INVOICE RECEIVED
        ↓
CASE CREATED
        ↓
REVIEW INVOICE
        ↓
WHAT DOES "REVIEW" ACTUALLY CHECK?
        ↓
CREATE VOUCHER
        ↓
WHAT CONDITIONS MUST BE SATISFIED?
        ↓
MAKE PAYMENT
        ↓
WHAT AUTHORIZES PAYMENT?
        ↓
COMPLETION
```

The research must search for:

- exact case template behavior;
- task dependencies;
- automated vs manual steps;
- approval rules;
- fields/data used;
- status transitions;
- notifications;
- integrations;
- exception branches;
- audit behavior;
- payment execution logic;
- implementation/customization strategy.

The objective is to produce a **usable workflow blueprint**, not merely another opportunity hypothesis.

